speechtext:
No; we take 75 per cent
under our contract, apart from what they pay in income tax; except for one thing, 14873-103}
which is a fixed fee, and that is something I am trying to get after; there is a fixed fee of so much per flying hour. Perhaps the flying hours are a little greater than was anticipated at the time they began, and they can make a reasonable profit. There is no revision of that, nor taking away of 75 per cent, but some companies have agreed to take 30 cents and some, 25 cents per flying hour as a fixed fee. Some are not taking anything.
